  "sign_rule": "InventoryLine.Quantity is signed by Sigma. DocType.TransferDoc = 1 → two lines: side 'out' (the From object, effect −qty) and side 'in' (the To object, effect +qty). DocType.InOut I+/I- → side 'in' (ClientTo/ObjectTo, effect +qty; a production input or a return to the supplier carries a negative qty). InOut O+/O- → side 'out' (ClientFrom/ObjectFrom, effect −qty; a customer return carries a negative qty). Lines are summed per (item_code, side); zero sums are dropped; qty has 3 decimals.",
  "client_name_rule": "client_name is sent only when the name looks like a company: one of company_hint_words appears as a WHOLE word (case-insensitive; a word = a run of letters), OR the name is one word, OR four words or more, OR it carries a digit or one of . * - & \" ( ). Otherwise null — a person's name never leaves the office. The same test runs in build_sigma_stock.py, the connector (lib/batch.mjs) and stock_sigma_ingest().",
